{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"29/07/2026 21:35:15","profile":{"player_id":"89235","last_updated":"29/07/2026 21:35","fullname":"Nahid Rana","short_display_name":"N Rana","name":"Nahid Rana","gender":"M","dob":"02/10/2002","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"Bangladesh","nationality_id":"2","nationality":"Bangladesh","nationality_short_code":"BAN","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"2","text":"Bowler","role":"Bowler"},"batting_style":{"id":"1","text":"Right Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"9","text":"Right-arm fast"},"writeup":"<p>Nahid Rana is a talented Bangladeshi cricketer and a formidable fast bowler who represents the Rajshahi Division in domestic cricket. Known for his raw pace and aggressive bowling, he holds the record for the fastest delivery by a Bangladeshi bowler in international cricket, clocking an impressive 152 kph.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p><br />\r\nHailing from the Chapai Nawabganj district, Nahid&rsquo;s cricketing journey began in 2020. After completing his Higher Secondary School Certificate that same year, he enrolled in a cricket academy in Rajshahi to refine his skills. Initially serving as a net bowler for Rajshahi Division, his ability to consistently bowl at high speeds quickly caught the attention of scouts.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p><br />\r\nNahid made his first-class debut for Rajshahi Division on October 31, 2021, in the National Cricket League. A year later, on the same date, he delivered a stunning performance, securing his maiden five-wicket haul against Barishal Division in the 2022&ndash;23 season. He finished the tournament as the second-highest wicket-taker, claiming 32 wickets.<br />\r\nHis growing reputation earned him a spot in the Khulna Tigers squad for the 2022&ndash;23 Bangladesh Premier League. Making his Twenty20 debut on January 24, 2023, he impressed immediately, bowling consistently between 140-150 km/h and taking a wicket for just 20 runs in his four-over spell. His List A debut followed on March 21, 2023, for Shinepukur Cricket Club in the Dhaka Premier Division Cricket League.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p><br />\r\nBy September 2023, Nahid&rsquo;s talent was recognized on a larger stage as he was named in Bangladesh&rsquo;s squad for the 2023 Asian Games. His rise continued in March 2024, when he earned his maiden call-up to the national Test squad for the series against Sri Lanka. He made his Test debut on March 22, 2024, showcasing his skills at the highest level.<br />\r\nA defining moment in his career came during Bangladesh&rsquo;s second Test against Pakistan, where he delivered a scorching 152.0 kph delivery, the fastest-ever by a Bangladeshi pacer in international cricket. In that series, 73 percent of his deliveries exceeded 140 kph, underlining his express pace. He played a crucial role in Bangladesh&rsquo;s historic victory, claiming four wickets in the second innings.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p><br />\r\nWith his rapid rise, exceptional pace, and ability to deliver under pressure, Nahid Rana has emerged as one of Bangladesh&rsquo;s most promising fast bowlers. As he continues to develop, he has the potential to be a game-changer for Bangladesh cricket on the global stage.&nbsp;</p>","relation":null,"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":{"trophy_details":[{"id":52,"name":"ICC Men's Player of the Month","number_of_times_won":1,"year":"Apr 2026","is_icc_award":true}]},"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"2","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"Bangladesh"},{"id":"805","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Rajshahi Division"},{"id":"1382","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Rangpur Riders"},{"id":"1400","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Bangladesh North Zone"},{"id":"1428","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Abahani Limited"},{"id":"1432","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Mohammedan Sporting Club"},{"id":"1514","active":"1","i